# Discord Bot Project - AI Assistant Rules

## Project structure

- **Root directory:** Only deployment config (package.json, railway.json, Procfile, .nvmrc, README.md, .cursorrules). No scripts, Python files, or bot code in root.
- **Bot code:** `xyian-bot-project/bot.js` — single file, the entire bot.
- **Knowledge:** `xyian-bot-project/data/knowledge.json` — curated game facts + custom facts added via Discord.
- **Feedback log:** `xyian-bot-project/data/feedback.json` — Q&A reaction feedback (auto-created).
- **Documentation:** `xyian-bot-project/docs/` — ENV reference, restart plan.
- **Archive:** `archive/` — old code kept for reference only. Never run or import from archive.

## Railway deployment

- Bot runs 24/7 on Railway. `npm start` runs `node xyian-bot-project/bot.js`.
- Daily reset (4pm Pacific) and guild recruit (every other day) run inside that process via setTimeout/setInterval.
- **Env vars** (set in Railway dashboard): `DISCORD_TOKEN`, `GENERAL_CHAT_WEBHOOK`, `GUILD_RECRUIT_WEBHOOK`, `ADMIN_WEBHOOK`, `OPENAI_API_KEY` (optional), `OWNER_ID` (optional).
- Do not remove the Express server or `/health` route (Railway healthcheck uses it).

## Channel behavior

- **#arch-ai** (ID `1424322391160393790`): Only channel where bot replies to normal messages. Requires verified role.
- **Guild recruit** (ID `1419944464608268410`): Bot never replies here. Only scheduled recruitment is sent via webhook.
- **General chat**: Only `!help`, `!menu`, `!ping` commands. No free-form replies.
- **Admin/debug**: Errors and events go to `ADMIN_WEBHOOK`.

## Roles

- Everyone: `!ping`, `!help`, `!menu`
- Verified (XYIAN Guild Verified, XYIAN OFFICIAL, Admin, Server Booster): Q&A, `!faq`, `!listfacts`
- Admin (XYIAN OFFICIAL, Admin): `!addfact`, `!removefact`, `!recruit`, `!reset`

## Workflow

- Update changelog after every completed task (`xyian-bot-project/CHANGELOG.md`).
- Keep bot.js as a single file. Only split into modules if it exceeds ~600 lines.
- Add docs to `xyian-bot-project/docs/` as needed.
